WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
Hello, everybody! My name is Markiplier!

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.740
And welcome back to Homecoming Starring Markiplier.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:08.740
Now we just got chased by a horrible monstrosity, or someone that turned INTO a horrible monstrosity.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:09.940
We're not sure which.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.580
"I dont need to go back to my room. It's easier to stay here, okay?"

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.560
Alright!

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.000
You stay  around the bloody toilets. I am sure they are fun and free and fancy.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.160
Okay. Hello!

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:23.929
"I used to be a painter. I mean I guess I
still am but.. I haven't made anything in so long."

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.380
Aww.. That's kinda sad.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.220
Being robbed of your skill. I mean, isn't the whole situation that these people are kinda in limbo,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.600
They're stuck between life, and death and that's no good?

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.160
*Chuckles* Chica, why are you chasing your tail over there? I'm sorry,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.860
Chica- Chica just caught my eye because, she just started chasing her tail randomly,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.220
She never really does that. Oh.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.220
"Why get out of bed if there's nothing you care to do? I should just go back to sleep."

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.780
Oh!

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.220
And roll over she did.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.780
Man, that sounds like depression symptoms.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
And that's no good.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.900
I mean, that would be odd if the people that were stuck in this limbo....

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.060
"It doesn't make any difference. Nothing will change anyway. Whats the point?"

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.300
That really sounds like depression

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.240
Is that why these people are stuck here?

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.080
Because they can't...

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.260
I don't know. They can't... find the motivation to move forward? The reason?

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.300
"I watched the sun rise this morning. I think I'm almost ready... to move up to floor five. It seems better there."

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.620
(Surprised) Oh!

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:20.920
Okay!

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.460
So some sort of... like...

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.220
Manual choice they have to do?

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.420
Like, they have to choose to ascend in this world?

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.420
Oh!

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.240
*Chuckles* It does seem better up here!

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.800
Oh this is lovely! &lt;3

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.720
It's very warm.. and golden!

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.400
"I don't hate it here, to be honest."

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.980
Well, don't you have a funky smile?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.620
"There are a lot of things I miss. But then there are a lot I don't."

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:43.720
Okay!

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.840
Thanks for being nice and vague!

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.360
I really wanted a lot of description here, and you didn't deliver at all.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.240
Okay.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.740
Hello! Who are you?

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.760
"He looked so determined when he came through. Do you think he'll succeed? It's possible, right?"

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.880
I...I don't know! You're all speaking so vaguely! I have no idea whats going on.

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:10.469
"I'm not here because I'm okay. I'm not okay, and I won't be. I'm just okay with never being okay now."

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:18.140
That's a cryptic way of looking at life, and existence, or non-existence or what ever else you want to call your time here.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.680
Chica's going nuts over there.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.260
Well someone wasn't very hungry.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.200
Hello teddy bear! Again...

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:24.500
Huh.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.120
"Probably lightens the mood."

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.260
I don't know! I seem to like all the MBBLLL-Blood downstairs.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.400
"Things could have gone another way, but they didn't. There are no alternate endings in life."

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.420
Huh. Well that's fancy!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.440
Well there might be alternate endings in this game! I mean, honestly, who knows?

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.800
Oh, are you the gate keeper?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.600
"I've totally accepted what I am. I have nothing deluding me, or holding me back anymore.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.680
Its that great?"

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.980
Oh is it people accepting their-

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.500
DDDDDD- OH!

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.940
"Why don't you become a monster too? You can stay here with us"

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.060
UH OH!  SORRY!

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.160
"Don't bother trying to escape"

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.240
I WILL BOTHER IMMEDIATELY!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.340
*scared laugh*

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.540
Hi, okay.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.760
🎵Goooooooooooooooood byyyyyyyee-EEeee🎵

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.540
Ha!

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.240
AWW!

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.940
I didn't... aw god damnit I didn't... awww

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.460
You bet. I'll try again.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.640
Is that the first time it's given me a try again? (no)

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.580
What am I supposed to do? HELP ME! *talks to girl* HELP ME!

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:22.560
Ohhh...

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.240
*Bleep*

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:30.080
*laughing* Jeeez! Nah, it's giving me a try again before but this one happens, happens to be very immediate.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.680
Oh boy, oh boy, oh boy. What do I do?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.460
It's not very clear!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.900
Not very clear!

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.400
Oh man that was quite the wicked hay maker.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.260
Cause I gotta get around to get back in to the upstairs in the next area but..

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:46.500
Whoa

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.700
Mark! I sense that you're struggling.. Let me help the best way I can.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.280
Uh tha... that... that be great

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:59.840
I'll show you the best path to take. You'll still have to travel it just right, to not be caught. I know you can do it!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.760
...iiing to escape!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.020
What? Fucking to escape? Ducking to escape? Plucking to es- Okay

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.460
Oh... Oooooh that is awfully handy

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:10.900
Thank you!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:17.280
Wait in here? What?! Oooh... *smack* Ooooooooh I didn't know that was a thing you could do.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.500
I mean I was gonna figure it it out but thanks for the conclusion... *mumbles everything else he was gonna say in english*.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.440
What ever...

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.100
Take your help and shove it up your butt.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.860
*Makes karate sounds*

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:28.360
K.O.!!!!!!

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.120
OH haha god damnit

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.260
Well that didn't help at all

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:33.260
*Its tea time!*

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:34.280
Wait no

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.820
AHHHHH YEEEEE AHHH YEEE AHHH YEEE

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.160
YEEEEEAAAAH!!! Good thing I'm so fast.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.400
Been getting a lot of training in my liiiiiiiiiiife that was too close

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.660
No thank you. Okay did I finally make it?

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.880
Let me make a savey soov

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:50.780
Alright

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.880
I got my save juice all over here.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:53.960
Lets see whats going on over here.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.860
Helloooooo

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.800
Ahh good. I know she's around here somewhere.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.300
*creep mode engaged

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:04.120
Come out, come out, where ever you are, Marki- hello?

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.560
"Uh oh..."

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.700
Uhhh... "Uh oh?"

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.160
"Are you a lingering spirit?"

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.420
"Me? No I'm alive... Like you."

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.480
"Am I?"

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.040
Ye... Yeah.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.920
"I guess it makes sense that you are. The nice lady on the fifth floor said it's hard for lingering spirits to ascend in the hospital."

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.880
"I thought you might have been on of the bad ones and you'd figured out how to get up here."

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:32.800
"Nah. I'm a friend. I was sent by your nurse actually. Nurse Hale. My name is Mark."

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:37.060
"Oh! New friends are nice, but I've known her for a long time. She's my best friend!"

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.140
"I think you're right about that. She saved your life by calling me here."

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.220
"How come?"

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:49.720
"Well.. What you're- what we're doing right now dangerous. We can only out of our for a while, and than we can never go back."

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:50.820
*lovely silence*

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:51.680
Oh...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:56.160
"I know it must be boring in your body, but Nurse Hale says they should be able to wake you up soon."

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:58.120
"She says that a lot.."

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:05.780
"I know she's trying as hard as she can, though. It just gets so boring. Maybe staying her as a spirit forever wouldn't be bad.."

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.120
"You don't want that. I've just met a lot of people in that situation, and trust me- they're not happy."

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:12.200
"hmmm"

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.740
*More silence*

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:18.120
"Will you stay and talk to me then? Just for a little while?"

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.880
"Of course! Let's go ahead and move to your room though, okay?"

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.120
"Okay!"

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:22.620
*says creepily*

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:26.200
And than get back into your bed and shove back into your fricken body!

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.380
So tell me about yourself, Sophie.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:33.320
Uh.. Well before the coma, it was just me and my dad. He was the nicest guy you'd ever meet!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:39.420
He was a brilliant doctor. He was so good, he inspired people around him to get into the health field too!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.800
He was a good cook, too. He would make me delicious dinners, and every morning he'd make me a different kind of sandwich.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.520
He didnt run out of ideas?

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:53.860
Oh, no. He would find recipes and sometimes just make something up. He'd always make an extra for Jenna, too. He was very nice.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.940
Sounds like he took very good care of you.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.020
Yep! And he will again... When he gets back.

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:00.840
Where is he?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.600
It's kind of a long story.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.820
Well, not like I'm in a hurry to save Tim.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:08.920
So, how long will I be asleep?

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.800
I don't know for sure, Bluebird. I'll be as diligent and quick as I can.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.400
Will I have dreams?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.680
Hmm.. I think you will.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.460
So I'll have nightmares too?

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:20.680
Let's hope not.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.420
Why can't I just go with you?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:28.820
Your condition is going to get much worse very soon. The only way I can prevent it is to put you to sleep for the time being.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.980
And than you'll wake me up when you can make me all better?

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:39.200
That's right. I'm very close to being able to cure you. I just have to make a trip to a far away place to use a special machine.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:40.620
Okay..

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.120
Don't worry. It'll all be over before you even realize it.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:46.940
Promise?

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.560
It'll be like it never happened.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.540
Something tells that promise was not kept. (no kidding Mark)

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:54.940
Are you ready?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.600
Yes Sir. I'm ready.

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:57.860
Very good.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.600
Screw being in a hospital!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.700
Right now our time is done.. but I will be the sun.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.060
Aww. I promise.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:07.260
*Markiplier thinks of all of the good times he had with his friends in horror games*

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:08.680
*remembers Tiny Box time and how adorable he was*

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.000
Did- Did he put her to sleep right then and there?

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.520
That's something we'd say whenever Daddy had to leave. The sun sets everyday, but no matter what happens, it always comes back.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.980
I see. And so you're still waiting on him to come back, huh?

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:26.620
Yeah. I know it's been a long time, but it's not his fault. He must have just ended up needing more time to find the cure.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:33.960
Well I hope he finds his way back to you soon. If he's not quick enough, Nurse Hale might just have you better before he gets here...

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:42.280
Hmm.. maybe. She's the nicest lady I know, but I don't think the regular doctors can cure me. Daddy said it was something really advanced.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:47.880
One way or another, they're gonna make you better. Until then, you need to stay put, okay? Even when it's kinda boring.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:49.960
Okay. I will.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:51.980
Mark?

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:52.960
Yeah?

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.320
Will you come back and see me sometime? Like this again, so we can talk?

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.620
To be honest.. I don't have much time left to spend as a spirit. A couple hours, maybe.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:09.100
But I'll tell you what.. as soon as I take care of little issue back home, I'll spend as much of that time as i can with you. Okay?

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.940
Okay! You have to be the sun!

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.240
Heh. I will. It was nice to meet you.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:15.340
You too!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.560
Well how will I know exactly how much time I have left?

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:23.760
I mean, I'm all for visiting you, but.. I don't know if i have that much time to go

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.080
Welcome back.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.420
Hiiiiiiiiiii!

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.180
Must've been a little crazy, huh?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:35.820
Yeah. It was a lot.. sadder than I expected. Scary or dangerous I'm used to by now, but I feel bad for all the lingering spirits...

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:43.380
Don't worry too much about them. They've only recently passed. Time is the best- and only- medicine for them. They'll pull out of it.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:50.460
Also, you may have found yourself to be a little moody as you ascended. The overall atmosphere of an area is determined by its residents

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:51.440
Ezzzz

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:58.680
This can affect how things look, as well as alter the mood of others who pass through. Did you notice a theme as you made your way?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.280
Yeah. It got brighter AS I WENT UP!

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:03.420
Anyways, there's good news!

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:03.980
Oh yeah?

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.800
It worked! Sophie's vitals looked so much better right away! I came down here, knowing you'd talked to her.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.580
That's great! She's such a sweet kid.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:15.280
We're gonna get her better. I won't rest a second until we do. Thank you so much for your help.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.840
I'm just happy that I was able to.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:21.840
Honestly, I'm a little jealous. I'm so fasinated with all this spiritual stuff...

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:25.060
SCREW MODERN MEDICINE, GET ME INTO SPIRITUALITY!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:28.580
...but I don't really like, I don't really get to experience it like you do.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:29.380
Oh well.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.140
Say uhh... What's the deal with Sophie's dad? She says he's away to research or something.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.680
Yeah, that was the last she heard before she fell into a coma. He's been missing for as long as she's been in the coma.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:46.820
Unfortunately, he is assumed to have passed. It's ashame too. He was a kind, brilliant man. He'd have her cured I bet...

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.640
Do you know what caused the coma?

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:55.860
We're not exactly sure, no. We figure it was most likely a side effect fo the stress caused by her condition.

00:10:55.860 --> 00:11:02.080
Hmm... Alright yeah because it's NOT! It's done did by her dad...

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:06.380
Well, I guess I should head home and take care of matters there, but I'll be back.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.380
I actually promised to spend more time with Sophie.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.200
Heh, you're very kind.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.960
Even though you're gonna get trapped in the spirit world, and your body's gonna wither away and die.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:16.700
*looks smugly at the camera* Oh well.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.480
If you don't mind my asking.. What is it that you have to take care of back home? I feel that I owe you.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.400
Well I've got a living weird creature of a BOX!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:29.500
It's cute and adorable but uh-  it talks and moves on its own!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:30.400
Very strange..

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:34.660
Uh- It's being chased by a.. body morphing, shapeshifting demon.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.300
*laughing* No! Not at all!

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.420
You don't owe me a thing, and I don't want you to get involved with thi- I WOULD!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:47.440
If someone's offering help to defeat a shape-shifting demon to rescue my little biscuit,

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.300
I would sure as hell recruit them!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.700
It's the demon- the same one that kicked me out of my body the first time.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.020
He's got a fake body, and is in my house.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.520
Oh, this is great!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.520
It doesn't sound great!

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.800
Say what? That's not the way I would describe it.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.200
I mean, not the demon. But I can help you out after all!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.880
Believe it or not, we can banish the demons from the safety of this creepy basement!

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:14.640
AW! OGOSH! I'm gonna uh- raise up my uh, questioning finger.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:17.160
I'm gonna press X to doubt on that one.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.280
Oh yeah?

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:23.500
In the time it would take you to drive home, I could teach you to project your spirit to a remote location.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.760
You could summon your helpers again.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.400
Oh!

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.400
You know- the monsters you used to get your body back the first time.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:35.460
A living spirit can do a lot of great things if
its wielder knows how.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.700
So it won't actually be here- be there?

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:40.340
I don't want to spend my remaining time
to be a wandering spirit

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:46.220
Mmm, your body would be here, but your spirit there. It would cost some of your remaining time, yes.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:50.120
But I can make it so you can speak with Sophie
from your body so that won't be an issue

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:56.300
other than people thinking you're
talking yours- How many superpowers do you have, lady?

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.920
